1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,480
 A $30,000 software that Wall Street has depended on for decades just got replaced by a free GitHub repo.

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:12,480
 Researchers from Tsinghua University just open-sourced an AI called Kronos,

3
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:18,140
 and it's the first foundation model ever built specifically to read the stock market like a language.

4
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:21,240
 Here's what makes this different from every trading bot you've seen.

5
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,560
 Kronos doesn't look at charts the way you do.

6
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:31,020
 It takes raw candlestick data, opens, closes, highs, lows, volume, and converts it into tokens.

7
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,140
 The same way ChatGPT turns words into tokens, except this isn't reading English.

8
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:38,740
 It's reading the language of financial markets.

9
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:42,960
 Kronos trained on data from over 45 stock exchanges around the world.

10
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:45,580
 Crypto, Forex, equities, and more.

11
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,460
 And the model? Completely free.

12
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:51,720
 Wall Street firms have spent billions building proprietary models like this,

13
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:54,360
 and a group of researchers just gave it away.

14
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:58,000
 This is the kind of thing that used to be locked behind hedge fund doors.

15
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:00,840
 Comment Kronos and I'll DM you the link.

